# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env (or .env.local) and adjust. Vite only exposes VITE_* variables.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the dashboard sends API requests.
#
#   /api                      → same-origin; Vite (dev) and Vercel (prod) proxy
#                               it to the host configured in vite.config.ts /
#                               vercel.json. Avoids CORS entirely. DEFAULT.
#   http://localhost:8080/api → talk to a local backend directly, bypassing the
#                               proxy. Requires the backend to allow this origin
#                               in config/cors.php (port 5173 is NOT allowed by
#                               default — see docs/api/decisions.md Q9).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Running the backend locally
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There is no deployed API (docs/api/probe-results.md). The backend runs from
# the sibling checkout with Docker:
#
#   cd ../4th_year_projects_refractored
#   docker compose up -d                                 # nginx :8080, mysql, redis
#   docker compose exec app1 php artisan migrate --seed  # seeds the system_admin
#
# That serves http://localhost:8080/api, which is what vite.config.ts proxies to
# and what the Postman collection's {{base_url}} expects.
